  "_comment": "Edit this file to add or change presets. Restart the app to pick up changes. 'accent2' is optional and is not drawn - it is offered in the colour dropdowns as that preset's 'highlight'. 'geometry' is 'steps' or 'curves'. 'scene' is 'town' or 'nature' and decides which silhouette styles the series can use - omit it and it is worked out from the series name, then from the geometry. 'suffix' is appended to the series name. 'cycle' is a list of colours the played line runs through, changing every 'cycle_minutes'. 'layouts' sets where the slate text sits and how big it is: 'landscape' is the 16:9 slate every render draws, 'vertical' is the 1080x1920 Shorts frame (--vertical). All positions and sizes are design units - the frame is 1280 wide in landscape and 'design_width' wide in vertical - so they describe a shape, not pixels. 'safe_top' and 'safe_bottom' are fractions of the frame height the vertical TEXT must stay out of; a line that enters one is an error naming it. Leave a field out and the built-in value is used.",
